content.text:
The profile pod is the root cause. I'm leaving out the search CPU rise: its own spans, error share and latency stayed flat, so its effect didn't leave the service.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "profile",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, metric, count(*) AS n, min(value) AS minv, max(value) AS maxv FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name = 'profile-599ff5546c-d7kv8' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.restarts', 'k8s.container.ready') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Profile pod restarts climb to 2-6 and k8s.container.ready stays 0 throughout the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) AS spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'profile' GROUP BY service_name", "claim": "Profile emits no spans at all in the abnormal window, versus about 4,750 in the normal window."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, round(avg(duration)/1e6, 3) AS avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name = 'profile.Profile/GetProfiles' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend's client calls to profile fail with Error status in about 0.01 ms, almost all of the 2,325 calls, with no connection made."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "profile", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name, c.span_name, p.span_name AS parent_span, p.attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id WHERE c.span_name = 'profile.Profile/GetProfiles' AND p.span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels', 'HTTP /recommendations') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Failed profile calls from frontend surface as HTTP 500s on /hotels and /recommendations."}]}
  ]
}
```
